From 0ae1ba5664b005e923ebaac9338c61675d83d621 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Azathothas <ajamx101@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:31:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] GitHub #739: pod-report.schema.json takes the backend
 netns-kernel

--backend netns-kernel is a real and documented backend, and its report
writes "backend": "netns-kernel". The schema is the contract: its enum
of backend now has netns-kernel. docs/pods.md names the value, and
udp_limit null for netns-kernel.

Test: tests/pod_report.rs exit_status_of_the_program_is_in_the_report
checks the report of each backend (netns, netns-kernel, seccomp)
against the schema.
---
 docs/pods.md                       |  6 +++---
 docs/schema/pod-report.schema.json |  6 +++---
 llms-full.txt                      |  6 +++---
 tests/pod_report.rs                | 22 ++++++++++++----------
 4 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/pods.md b/docs/pods.md
index 236451d..64aecd8 100644
--- a/docs/pods.md
+++ b/docs/pods.md
@@ -149,10 +149,10 @@ podnet pod -x socks5://127.0.0.1:1080 \
 
 * `--report FILE` writes one JSON object to FILE when the pod starts, and again when it ends. Each write
   replaces the file with a rename of a temporary file in the same directory. The mode is 0600.
-* The keys: `schema` (1), `version` (of podnet), `backend` (`netns`, `seccomp` or null), `choice` (the reason
-  of the choice), `hold` (`enforced`, `advisory` or `none`: the words of `podnet pod doctor --json`),
+* The keys: `schema` (1), `version` (of podnet), `backend` (`netns`, `netns-kernel`, `seccomp` or null),
+  `choice` (the reason of the choice), `hold` (`enforced`, `advisory` or `none`: the words of `podnet pod doctor --json`),
   `not_held` (the ways out that the backend does not hold), `udp_limit` (the most bytes of a UDP datagram:
-  65507 for `netns`, null for `seccomp`), `exit` and `reason`.
+  65507 for `netns`, null for `netns-kernel` and `seccomp`), `exit` and `reason`.
 * `exit` is null in the first write. In the last write it is the exit status of `podnet pod`. `reason` is
   the cause of a failure (exit 64 or 3), else null.
 * A pod that cannot start writes the report with `backend` null, `hold` `none` and its `reason`. Exit 3 of a
